Week 2: Intermediate Java Problem Solving & Matrix Operations
1) Matrix & 2D Array Structures: Declaring and manipulating 2D arrays and jagged arrays (arrays of arrays with varying row
lengths).
2) 2D Array Transformations: In-place matrix operations: matrix transposition, 90° clockwise and counter-clockwise
transformations, diagonal indexing, and spiral matrix traversals.
3) Conditional 2D Search Algorithms: Optimizing search logic inside row-wise and column-wise sorted matrices using
Staircase Search algorithms in O(M + N) time complexity.
4) Two-Pointer Algorithmic Frameworks: Opposite-directional two-pointer loops for target sum matching in sorted arrays;
same-directional fast/slow pointers for array partitioning and cycle detection.
5) Sliding Window Techniques: Fixed-length and variable-length sliding window patterns for tracking maximum subarray
sums, minimum window substrings, and contiguous subarray metrics.
6) Bitwise Operations & Masks: Direct bit manipulations using Java operators (&, |, ^, ~). Bit shift mechanics: Left Shift (<<),
Arithmetic Right Shift (>>), and Unsigned Logical Right Shift (>>>).
7) Bitwise Algorithmic Optimization: Fast exponentiation using bit-shifting loops, parity checking, and isolating the rightmost
set bit using two's complement arithmetic (X & -X).
8) Hashing Mechanics & Hash Contracts: The Java hashing specification: overriding hashCode() and equals() contracts
properly.
HashMap Internals: Internal architecture of java.util.HashMap: Bucket array indexing, load factor mechanics, dynamic
rehashing, collision resolution via separate chaining, and Red-Black tree conversion (TREEIFY_THRESHOLD = 8).
